# =============================================================================
# Users — PROFILE requests (VS Code REST Client) — GET /api/v1/users/profile
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use — later requests assume earlier ones ran.
#   - All data is FAKE (test personas, devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: UsersApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send the latest login request (### 2 for Ada, ### 14 for Chidi) to
#     refresh the chained tokens, then continue.
#   - Expected codes: 200 self profile, 401 no/invalid/revoked/expired token, 405 wrong
#     method, 204 logout.
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/users
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: signup Ada (profile persona)
# Expected: 201
# @name adaSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada Obi",
  "email": "ada.profile@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234567"
}

### 2 — Setup: login Ada, capture both tokens
# Expected: 200
# @name adaLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada.profile@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3 — Read own profile with a valid token
# Expected: 200 — publicId, fullName "Ada Obi", email, phone E.164, role ROLE_USER
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile

### 5 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 6 — Raw JWT without the "Bearer " prefix
# Expected: 401 — the filter only accepts the Bearer scheme
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7 — Wrong auth scheme (Basic) with the JWT in it
# Expected: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Basic {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Wrong method: POST to /profile
# Expected: 405 — only GET is mapped
POST {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9 — Wrong method: PUT to /profile (also proves profile is read-only for now)
# Expected: 405
PUT {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Hacker McEditface"}

### 10 — THE JTI PROBE, step 1: logout Ada
# Expected: 204 — revokes the access-token jti and burns the refresh family.
# This is the end-to-end revocation check ticket 0004 predicted: the profile
# route was the first protected route that made it probeable.
POST {{authUrl}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{adaLogin.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 11 — THE JTI PROBE, step 2: read profile with the dead token
# Expected: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12 — Second persona, setup: signup Chidi
# Expected: 201
# @name chidiSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Chidi Okafor",
  "email": "chidi.profile@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234568"
}

### 13 — Second persona, setup: login Chidi
# Expected: 200
# @name chidiLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "chidi.profile@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 14 — Profile returns THE CALLER's data, never someone else's
# Expected: 200 — email is chidi.profile@devtunde.com (self), not Ada's
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{chidiLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
